# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Text files are stored with LF inside the repository.  What lands in your working
# copy is left alone -- no eol= is set, so Git checks out whatever your core.autocrlf
# and core.eol say, and a Windows contributor still gets CRLF on disk if that is how
# their Git is configured.  Only the committed bytes are pinned.
#
# This is here because the tree arrived with mixed endings.  The files came through
# upstream CountryValidator and then three repair waves on different machines, and
# six test files are still CRLF on disk against 184 that are LF:
#
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/IndonesiaValidatorTests.cs
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/JapanValidatorTests.cs
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/KoreaValidatorTests.cs
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/PakistanValidatorTests.cs
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/PhilippinesValidatorTests.cs
#   Attest.Tests/CountriesValidators/SloveniaValidatorTests.cs
#
# That is where "CRLF will be replaced by LF" comes from when you stage one of them.
# The warning is the normalisation working, not an error, and it stops once those
# six are rewritten in the index.  To clear it, the maintainer runs
#
#   git add --renormalize .
#
# and commits the result on its own, so the whitespace churn is never mixed into a
# commit that also changes a check-digit rule or an InlineData row.

* text=auto

# The three text types this repository is made of.  diff=csharp gives hunk headers
# that name the enclosing method, which is the difference between a readable diff
# and an unreadable one when 87 validator files share the same method names.
*.cs   text diff=csharp
*.md   text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text

# Build inputs.
*.csproj  text
*.props   text
*.targets text
*.sln     text

# Binary.  None of these are in the tree today; the entries are here so that a
# signing key, an icon for the NuGet package, or a downloaded .nupkg added later is
# never run through line-ending normalisation, which would corrupt it silently.
*.snk   binary
*.nupkg binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
